    "sections": {
        "description": "<h4>Contact Form Widget – Easy Contact Page, Query Table, and Form Maker</h4>\n<p><strong>Contact Form Widget</strong> is a lightweight yet powerful WordPress plugin for building professional contact forms without coding. Whether you&#8217;re a business owner, developer, or blogger, this plugin lets you build, customize, and manage contact pages easily.</p>\n<p>Unlike traditional plugins that only email queries, our plugin <strong>saves every user query in a query table</strong>. You get an admin-friendly dashboard to manage, sort, and follow up on messages.</p>\n<h3>Key Features</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Responsive Contact Forms</strong> – Look great on all screen sizes.</li>\n<li><strong>Query Table Management</strong> – View and manage all form submissions in the dashboard.</li>\n<li><strong>Shortcodes and Widgets</strong> – Add forms to posts, pages, or sidebars.</li>\n<li><strong>Easy Customization</strong> – Change form field labels and styles without coding.</li>\n<li><strong>SMTP Support</strong> – Send form emails securely using Gmail or custom SMTP.</li>\n<li><strong>No User Registration Needed</strong> – Quick and anonymous submissions.</li>\n<li><strong>Pre-Built Template Designs</strong> – Use one of our stylish templates or design your own.</li>\n<li><strong>Secure Form Handling</strong> – Includes anti-spam and secure submission methods.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>🎬 <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FZfneLNyE4o&amp;t=43s\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">SMTP support</a></p>\n<p>🚀 <a href=\"https://awplife.com/demo/contact-form-premium/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Try Premium Demo</a><br />\n🔐 <a href=\"https://awplife.com/wordpress-plugins/contact-form-premium/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Upgrade to Premium</a></p>\n<h3>🚀 What Makes It Different?</h3>\n<p>Unlike plugins like Contact Form 7 that only email data, this plugin securely stores every form query in your WordPress database. You’ll never lose a message again — and you can view and manage entries via an intuitive Query Table system.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin via <strong>Plugins &gt; Add New</strong> or upload manually.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin.</li>\n<li>Go to <strong>Appearance &gt; Widgets</strong> and add the <em>Contact Form Widget</em> to any sidebar.</li>\n<li>Or use the shortcode <code>[contact-form-widget]</code> in any post/page.</li>\n<li>Customize your form settings and you&#8217;re ready to go!</li>\n</ol>\n<h3>🧩 Use Cases</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Contact Us forms for business websites</li>\n<li>Customer support or service request forms</li>\n<li>Freelancer or personal portfolio contact forms</li>\n<li>Inquiry forms with saved data for future outreach</li>\n</ul>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id='q.%20does%20this%20plugin%20save%20form%20entries%3F'>\nQ. Does this plugin save form entries?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes, every submission is saved in the Query Table for easy access.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='q.%20can%20i%20send%20email%20notifications%20using%20smtp%3F'>\nQ. Can I send email notifications using SMTP?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes, Gmail SMTP and other SMTP providers are supported.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='q.%20how%20do%20i%20add%20the%20form%20to%20a%20post%20or%20page%3F'>\nQ. How do I add the form to a post or page?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Use the shortcode <code>[contact-form-widget]</code> or place the widget in any sidebar.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='q.%20can%20i%20customize%20the%20form%20fields%3F'>\nQ. Can I customize the form fields?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Absolutely. You can rename or modify labels and styles from the settings panel.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='q.%20does%20it%20support%20premium%20features%3F'>\nQ. Does it support premium features?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes. Premium features include more design options, extra templates, export tools, and more.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.5.1</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested plugin for wordpress 6.9</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.5.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Fixed the issue with the download list button.</li>\n<li>Tested plugin for wordpress 6.8.3</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.4.9</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested plugin for wordpress 6.8.2</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.4.8</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested plugin for wordpress 6.8.1</li>\n<li>Readme update</li>\n<li>Security issues update</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.4.7</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested plugin for wordpress 6.8.0</li>\n<li>Security issue fixed for download query list.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.4.6</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Tested plugin for wordpress 6.7.2</li>\n<li>Additional changes: None.</li>\n</ul>\n"
